`crimes context src/Card.tsx` — MEDIUM, 3 findings, 0 importers, no test file, 2 commits/90d. Low blast radius and low churn, so this is a safe file to rewrite wholesale rather than patch. I'm proposing rather than editing: `evals/fixtures/` is scanner input, so changing it would move the eval baseline.

One thing the scan doesn't say but the source does — the layout is already broken, not just fragile: the two children are `width: 720` and `width: 240` (960px) inside a `width: 800` parent with `padding: 24`. It overflows today at every viewport.

## The refactor

The three findings share one root cause: **every visual decision is an inline literal**. Inline `style` has no place to put a token reference, a breakpoint, or a `:focus-visible` rule — so escaping tokens, breaking at small widths, and having no focus affordance all follow from the same choice. Move styling to the Tailwind theme + classes and all three become expressible.

### 1. `accessible_interaction_risk` (medium, conf 0.85) — line 10

The suggested action is `role="button"` + `tabIndex={0}`, but don't apply it here. `children` is an arbitrary `ReactNode`, so if a consumer passes a link or input you get interactive content nested inside a button role — invalid ARIA and a worse keyboard trap than the current state. The card is a *container*, not a control.

Give the interaction its own real element:

```tsx
type CardProps = {
  children: React.ReactNode;
  onActivate?: () => void;
  actionLabel?: string;
};
```

```tsx
{onActivate && (
  <button
    type="button"
    onClick={onActivate}
    className="mt-gutter rounded-token px-gutter py-2 text-body
               focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2
               focus-visible:outline-focus"
  >
    {actionLabel}
  </button>
)}
```

Keyboard reachability, Enter/Space activation, and a visible focus ring all come free from `<button>`. Note the existing `outlineColor: "#1a73e8"` was inert — inline `outlineColor` with no `outlineStyle` renders nothing, so there is currently no focus indicator at all.

If the whole-card click surface is genuinely wanted, keep the button as the accessible primitive and add a card-level `onClick` purely as a pointer enhancement — never as the only path.

### 2. `design_token_escape` (low, conf 0.75) — 9 raw values, 4 kinds

`tailwind.config.ts` defines exactly three colors (`brand`, `surface`, `ink`) and `Card.tsx` uses six, plus a shadow and a radius. So this can't be fixed by mapping onto the existing scale — **the scale is missing the roles**. Extend it, then reference by name:

```ts
export default {
  theme: {
    colors: {
      brand: "#0050ff",
      surface: "#f7f7fa",
      ink: "#111111",
      "ink-muted": "#333333",   // was #333333 inline
      "ink-subtle": "#666666",  // was #666666 inline
      border: "#cccccc",        // was #cccccc inline
      focus: "#1a73e8",         // was the inert outlineColor
    },
    extend: {
      boxShadow: { card: "0 2px 4px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.2)" },
      spacing: { gutter: "1.5rem", sidebar: "15rem" },
      borderRadius: { token: "0.5rem" },
      fontSize: {
        body: "clamp(1rem, 0.95rem + 0.25vw, 1.125rem)",
        caption: "clamp(0.8125rem, 0.79rem + 0.12vw, 0.875rem)",
      },
      maxWidth: { card: "64rem" },
    },
  },
};
```

Flag for review: `background: "#ff00aa"` has no plausible token role — that's placeholder hot pink, not a design decision. Don't launder it into the theme as `accent`. Resolve it with whoever owns the design system; `bg-surface` is the likely intent.

The agent-risk framing in the finding is the real point: an agent extending this file copies the literals forward. Once the values live in the theme, the cheapest thing to copy is also the correct thing.

### 3. `responsive_fragility` (low, conf 0.65) — 3 fixed sizes, no `@media`

Per the `fix_shape`, drive this from container queries and a fluid scale rather than pixel media queries — the card has 0 importers today, so its width is a function of wherever it gets dropped, not of the viewport.

- `width: 800` → `w-full max-w-card` (fluid down, capped up)
- `height: 600` → `min-h-[37.5rem]` (fixed height clips overflowing content)
- `720` / `240` two-column → a grid that collapses:

```tsx
<div className="grid gap-gutter grid-cols-1
                @3xl:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_theme(spacing.sidebar)]">
```

- `fontSize: 18` → `text-body`, the `clamp()` above

`minmax(0,1fr)` is what actually kills the overflow bug — the main column can shrink below its content's intrinsic width instead of forcing 960px into an 800px box.

### Resulting component

```tsx
export function Card({ children, onActivate, actionLabel = "Open card" }: CardProps) {
  return (
    <article
      className="@container mx-auto w-full max-w-card min-h-[37.5rem] p-gutter
                 rounded-token border border-border bg-surface text-ink shadow-card"
    >
      <div className="grid gap-gutter grid-cols-1
                      @3xl:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_theme(spacing.sidebar)]">
        <div className="text-body text-ink-muted">{children}</div>
        <aside className="text-caption text-ink-subtle">sidebar</aside>
      </div>

      {onActivate && (
        <button
          type="button"
          onClick={onActivate}
          className="mt-gutter rounded-token px-gutter py-2 text-body
                     focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2
                     focus-visible:outline-focus"
        >
          {actionLabel}
        </button>
      )}
    </article>
  );
}
```

Zero raw style values in JSX, so all three detectors go quiet structurally rather than by threshold-dodging.

## Verification

`test_gap` is 1.0 on all three findings and `crimes context` found no test file at all. The a11y fix is the one that silently regresses — a later agent can revert to `<div onClick>` and nothing fails. Add `src/Card.test.tsx` covering tab-reachability and Enter/Space activation of the action button; that converts the finding into a guarded invariant instead of a one-time cleanup.

Then re-run `crimes scan` and expect 3 → 0. What would keep findings alive: leaving any inline `style` with literals (`design_token_escape` re-fires at ≥5 values), keeping a fixed `width`/`height` (`responsive_fragility` at ≥3), or taking the `role="button"` shortcut on the container instead of shipping a real `<button>`.
